Large-ROM PI decode fix for the ares test harness (apply on top of
ares-testharness.patch).

Why: the patched ares force-enables the ISViewer debug channel at PI
0x13ff0000 even when the cartridge image is bigger than 0x3ff0000
(64 MiB - 64 KiB) — that is how a >64 MiB ROM still gets its log lines to
stdout. ISViewer's 64 KiB window then swallows cart ROM data: every asset
stored in ROM offsets 0x3ff0000-0x3ffffff reads back as ISViewer RAM (zeros),
which shows up as e.g.

  Sys_Error: Mod_LoadBrushModel: models/w_suit.mdl has wrong version number
             (0 should be 29 or 30)

(the model's IDST ident reads as 0). The test-harness peripheral at
0x13fe0000 has the same problem for its 4 KiB window, and it is decoded even
when ARES_TEST_HARNESS is unset.

Fix: only the device *register* pages are taken from the device on reads; the
rest of each window falls through to the cartridge when the ROM covers it.
Device writes are untouched, so ISViewer logging and the harness protocol
(TH_Present reads the magic at 0x13fe0010) keep working.

Residual: 32 bytes of ROM are shadowed at each register page
(0x13fe0000-0x13fe001f and 0x13ff0000-0x13ff001f). With the current content
set those land inside models/v_shotgun.stb2 and models/w_shotgunt.mdl; they
move with any content change, so keep ROM data the ROM polls out of them.

diff --git a/ares/n64/pi/bus.hpp b/ares/n64/pi/bus.hpp
--- a/ares/n64/pi/bus.hpp
+++ b/ares/n64/pi/bus.hpp
@@ -45,10 +45,26 @@ inline auto PI::busRead(u32 address) -> u32 {
     if(cartridge.flash) return cartridge.flash.read<Size>(address);
     return unmapped;
   }
-  if(cartridge.isviewer.enabled() && address >= 0x13ff'0000 && address <= 0x13ff'ffff) {
+  //ISViewer (dev cart) lives at PI 0x13ff0000-0x13ffffff: registers at
+  //0x13ff0000-0x13ff001f, write-only buffer above. A cartridge image larger
+  //than 0x3ff0000 (64 MiB - 64 KiB) covers that range, and the
+  //harness/ARES_ISVIEWER path force-enables the device at any ROM size (so
+  //homebrew with a fat ROM can still log). Only the register reads may come
+  //from the device (libdragon probes the magic at +0x00, libultra reads the
+  //buffer pointers); the buffer half of the window is cart data, otherwise
+  //every asset stored there reads back as ISViewer RAM (zeros).
+  if(cartridge.isviewer.enabled()
+  && ((address >= 0x13ff'0000 && address <= 0x13ff'001f)
+   || (address >= 0x13ff'0020 && address <= 0x13ff'ffff
+    && address > 0x1000'0000 + cartridge.rom.size - 1))) {
     return cartridge.isviewer.read<Size>(address);
   }
-  if(address >= 0x13fe'0000 && address <= 0x13fe'0fff) {
+  //Test harness: registers at 0x13fe0000-0x13fe001f (only +0x10 is readable),
+  //rest of the 4 KiB window is scratch. As with ISViewer above, a ROM larger
+  //than 64 MiB reaches into this window, so only the register block is taken
+  //from the device; the remaining bytes stay cart data.
+  if(address >= 0x13fe'0000 && address <= 0x13fe'0fff
+  && (address <= 0x13fe'001f || address > 0x1000'0000 + cartridge.rom.size - 1)) {
     cartridge.testharness.load();  //idempotent; enables it on DD-only boots
     if(cartridge.testharness.enabled()) {
       if constexpr(Size == Word) return cartridge.testharness.readWord(address);
